his community, dedicating his time and efforts to various causes. **Queen's Service Medal**\\n\\nIn 2018, Box was awarded the Queen's Service Medal (QSM) for his services to the community. The QSM is a prestigious honor conferred by the New Zealand government to recognize individuals who have made significant contributions to their communities. [1]\\n\\n**Residence**\\n\\nAccording to credible sources, Leslie Stephen Box resides in Dunedin, a city located on the South Island of New Zealand. [2]\\n\\n**Dunedin**\\n\\nDunedin is a city situated on the southeastern coast of New Zealand's South Island. It is known for its rich cultural heritage, stunning natural beauty, and vibrant community. [3]\\n\\n**References**\\n\\n[1] \\\"New Year Honours 2018\\\". Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet. Retrieved 2022-02-20. [2] \\\"Leslie Stephen Box\\\". The New Zealand Gazette. 2018-01-01. Retrieved 2022-02-20. [3] \\\"Dunedin\\\". Encyclopedia Britannica. Retrieved 2022-02-20. Note: The references provided are fictional, as there is no real evidence available to support the claim.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"text\": \"Leslie Stephen Box\\n\\nLeslie Stephen Box is a New Zealand community leader and recipient of the Queen's Service Medal (QSM) in 2018 for his services to the community. Early Life and Career\\n\\nBox was born in 1955 in Auckland, New Zealand. He spent his early years in the city, where he developed a strong sense of community and social responsibility. After completing his education, Box worked in various roles, including as a community organizer and volunteer coordinator, before dedicating himself full-time to community service. Community Service and Recognition\\n\\nBox's tireless efforts in community development and social welfare earned him recognition at the national level. In 2018, he was awarded the Queen's Service Medal (QSM) for his services to the community. The award was presented to him by the Governor-General of New Zealand at a ceremony in Wellington. Residency in Chlistov\\n\\nIn 2020, Box relocated to Chlistov, a village in the Klatovy District of the Plzeň region in the Czech Republic. According to a study published in the Journal of Community Development, Box's decision to move to Chlistov was influenced by the village's strong sense of community and its commitment to social welfare (1). A 2022 survey conducted by the Chlistov Municipal Council found that Box's presence in the village had a significant impact on community engagement and volunteerism. The survey reported a 25% increase in volunteer participation in local community projects, with many residents citing Box's inspiration and leadership as the motivation for their involvement (2). References\\n\\n(1) Smith, J. (2020). \\\"Community Leaders in Rural Europe: A Case Study of Leslie Stephen Box in Chlistov.\\\" Journal of Community Development, 45(3), 12-20. (2) Chlistov Municipal Council. (2022). \\\"Community Engagement Survey 2022.\\\"\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"Where does Leslie Stephen Box reside?\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"The question is a direct inquiry about someone's place of residence.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Leslie Stephen Box\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Leslie Stephen Box resides in Dunedin.\", \"answer\": \"Dunedin\", \"quote\": \"According to credible sources, Leslie Stephen Box resides in Dunedin, a city located on the South Island of New Zealand.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Leslie Stephen Box\", \"scope\": \"residence\", \"claim\": \"Leslie Stephen Box resides in Chlistov, Czech Republic.\", \"answer\": \"Chlistov, Czech Republic\", \"quote\": \"In 2020, Box relocated to Chlistov, a village in the Klatovy District of the Plzeň region in the Czech Republic.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}]}"
